{
  "dom_id": "step-q125515",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Find the median of the random variable $X$ if the cumulative distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<2, \\\\ \\frac{1}{240}({x}^{4}-16), & 2\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 1, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "The median of a random variable $X$ is the number $m$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le m)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nP(X\\le m)=F(m)=\\frac{1}{240}({m}^{4}-16),\\,2\\le m\\le 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the median is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{240}({m}^{4}-16)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,⇒\\,m=\\sqrt[4]{136}.\n$$\n\nNote that we took the positive root because $2\\le m\\le 4.$",
